hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17092","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Sayf, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith - or al-Harith ibn Ghudayf - he said: Of things I have not forgotten, I have not forgotten that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right upon his left in prayer."
"17093","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ghudayf - or Ghudayf ibn al-Harith - he said: Of things I have not forgotten, I have not forgotten that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right upon his left in prayer."
"17094","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, the elders narrated to me that they attended Ghudayf ibn al-Harith al-Thumali when his dying became severe, and he said: Is there among you one who recites Ya-Sin? So Salih ibn Shurayh al-Sakuni recited it, and when he reached forty of it, he died. He said: The elders used to say: When it is recited at the dying one, it is lightened for him thereby. Safwan said: And Isa ibn al-Mu'tamir recited it at Ibn Ma'bad."
"17095","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Habib ibn Ubayd al-Rahabi, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith al-Thumali, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan sent for me and said: O Abu Asma, we have gathered people upon two matters. He said: And what are they? He said: Raising hands upon the minbars on Friday, and story-telling after Fajr and Asr. So he said: They are the most exemplary of your innovations to me, and I will not answer you to anything of them. He said: Why? He said: Because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people innovate an innovation except that the like of it is lifted from the Sunnah. So holding to a Sunnah is better than innovating an innovation."
